  "result": "`click.KeyValue` is added and tests pass (`tests/test_types.py`: 47 passed, 2 skipped; I did not run the full suite).\n\n- **Behavior:** `click.KeyValue()` splits on the first `=` and returns a `(key, value)` tuple, so `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")` and `a=` gives `(\"a\", \"\")`. Input with no `=` or with an empty key fails with `'...' is not a valid key=value pair.`.\n- **Code:** the class sits after `UUIDParameterType` in `src/click/types.py` and is exported in `src/click/__init__.py`.\n- **Tests:** I added valid and invalid cases at the end of `tests/test_types.py`.",
